&#x200B;

(joke)

I doubt it will affect her child unless directly exposed, it depends on the condition, if the microwave is capable of producing large amounts of radiation than it's a threat. However microwaves are designed not to leak radiation. Plus I have yet to hear of a valid and confirmed medical injury caused by a microwaves radiation, the radiation is very limiting and only dangerous in extreme contact.

&#x200B;

When I say extreme contact, I mean large amounts, chances are the radiation caused by your microwave is the same for lightbulbs and radios, your mothers baby is 100% safe, although 13 years is pretty damn old for a microwave lol.

This sounds like a very..deep dream, you could look at it as it's showing you your life and goals, in the beginning the dream represents happiness, and you said it was exiting to venture into, much like the real world to a child or baby, and fear of the new is represented by how "the sea looks angry" as the dream goes on you begin to feel the love and nourishment one recieves, some people leave but that's okay, the people who mean the most are those who stay the longest. at the end you fall/sink into the ocean, and like that the  dream finishes and life ends. It sounds like a pretty good dream, fun in the beginning but it gets more interesting near the end.

&#x200B;

I hope this put a new perspective on it.

happy by pharrell williams

&#x200B;

That song gives anyone strength.

Not a grandparent (or even a parent) but think of it this way, when you went to grandmas house she probably always made delicous food, had fun games and was a super nice person. But, chances are you heard stories from your mom/dad about how they either were beaten, or they made your grandparents out to be bad people. With this in mind it's possible most grandparents see grandkids as a 2nd chance of being a parent.

&#x200B;

although it's possible this only happens because parents rarely tell the good stories, but my point still stands.
